cy / power_supply_option:\n{\"condition\": \"external AC supply (tolerance ±2 %)\", \"value\": {\"min\": 50, \"max\": 60}, \"unit_symbol\": \"Hz\"}\n\ntype_level:\nmeasuring_principle: {\"value\": \"Electromagnetic\", \"unit_symbol\": null}\naccuracy_class: {\"value\": \"1 and 2\", \"unit_symbol\": null}\nmechanical_environment: {\"value\": \"M2\", \"unit_symbol\": null}\nelectromagnetic_environment: {\"value\": \"E2\", \"unit_symbol\": null}\nwater_temperature_class: {\"value\": \"T50\", \"unit_symbol\": null}\nwater_temperature_range: {\"value\": {\"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 50}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"}\nmaximum_admissible_pressure: {\"value\": 1.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"MPa\"}\norientation: {\"value\": \"All positions (horizontal, vertical or diagonal)\", \"unit_symbol\": null}\nflow_profile_sensitivity_class: {\"value\": \"U0 and D0\", \"unit_symbol\": null}\nstraight_length_requirement: {\"value\": \"0 x DN upstream and 0 x DN downstream\", \"unit_symbol\": null}\nreverse_flow: {\"value\": \"The sensor is designed to measure reverse flow\", \"unit_symbol\": null}\npressure_loss_class: {\"value\": \"Δp 63\", \"unit_symbol\": null}\nmaximum_pressure_loss: {\"value\": 0.63, \"unit_symbol\": \"bar\"}\n\nOK. Now output. No fences, no commentary. Actually... should I add a tiny note? The instruction is explicit: \"Return the SAME object as one valid JSON object with all internal quotes properly escaped, nothing added or removed, no markdown fences.\" I'll return just the JSON.\n\nOne consideration: JSON validity requires proper number formats. \"0.0001\", \"3.9375\" etc. are fine. \"page_total\": 6 fine.\n\nLet me now assemble the final answer meticulously.",
